// The cotangent of a read, answered from the **type**.
//
// `pick` reads one element of its parameter, so the cotangent of that parameter is a zero array of
// its shape with one slot filled. `transpose` answers one cotangent per parameter and passes nothing
// else -- every parameter is a linear input (design principles 9.9) -- so the transposed function is
// handed the cotangent and *no* value of `x`.
//
// The shape that zero array needs is not a value: it is a fact `x: float[3]` states, and the walk
// fills the port `rulesets/transpose.cml#idx_arr_t` names with the shape it reads off that type
// (`modules/transforms/transpose.cpp#shapeFromTypeOf`, the one reading of
// `camel::core::type::statedExtentsOf`), so the law builds its zeros with `zeros_of(ct,
// extent_product(at))` and the answer is `([0.0, 1.0, 0.0])` on both back ends -- the adjoint of
// `x[1]` at ct = 1 fills slot 1 and every other slot is zero.
//
// Before this case's change the difference reached the run as a count, and a count is not a report:
//
//   error[...]: Pass 'std::nvm' failed with an internal error: Runtime indirect call norm-arity
//   mismatch: caller graph 'main' node 3 has 1 args, target graph 'transpose_of_pick' has 2 norm
//   ports.
//   help: ... which is a defect of the compiler rather than of the program. ... report the program
//   together with the pass list.
//
// on `std::nvm`, whose help asked a reader to report their own program as a defect of the compiler,
// and an abort on the fast VM (`FastVM indirect call norm-arity mismatch for graph
// 'transpose_of_pick': expected 2, got 1`, exit 134). None of those sentences may come back, and
// this case pins the answer above instead of a count.
//
// A parameter whose type states **no** extents (`float[...]`) is the other side of the same rule: no
// law can state the length, so the build refuses by name
// (`RuntimeDiag::TransposeNeedsParameterShape`, pinned by `transpose_needs_parameter_shape`).
import { transpose } from transforms
import rulesets.transpose

func pick(x: float[3]): float {
    return x[1]
}

func main(): int sync {
    let back = transpose(pick)
    println(back(1.0))
    return 0
}